  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Taeyeon has a large collection of NNN pretty boxes (numbered 111 through NNN). For each valid iii, the iii-th box has two attributes SiS_iSi​ and PiP_iPi​, representing the size and beauty of the box respectively, and it can fit inside each box jjj such that Si≤SjS_i \\le S_jSi​≤Sj​. (Don't ask why a box can fit into another box with the same size.)\n\nYoona's birthday is coming very soon, so Taeyeon decided to give Yoona some boxes as birthday gifts. As it is not cool to gift empty boxes, Taeyeon decided to put boxes inside boxes. Specifically, Taeyeon wants to choose KKK pairs of boxes (for some valid KKK) and for each pair, put one box inside the other (if they have the same size, she can choose which box should be inside; otherwise, she puts the smaller box inside the bigger one). For each pair of boxes (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that box iii is inside box jjj, the beauty of this pair is Pj−PiP_j - P_iPj​−Pi​, since Taeyeon would think the beauty of the inner box is wasted.\n\nUnboxing boxes is very tiring, so it is possible that Yoona does not want many pairs of boxes, and Taeyeon does not know the ideal value of KKK. Therefore, for each KKK between 111 and ⌊N2⌋\\left\\lfloor\\frac{N}{2}\\right\\rfloor⌊2N​⌋, you need to help Taeyeon find the maximum possible total beauty she could obtain using at most KKK pairs of boxes (the maximum possible sum of beauties of these pairs).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Si≤2⋅1051 \\le S_i \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤Si​≤2⋅105 for each valid iii",
      "1≤Pi≤1091 \\le P_i \\le 10^91≤Pi​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):** N≤100N \\le 100N≤100",
      "**Subtask #2 (30 points):** N≤3,000N \\le 3,000N≤3,000",
      "Example Input 1`3",
      "1 4",
      "3 1",
      "4 5",
      "`Example Output 1`4",
      "`Example Input 2`5",
      "1 4",
      "1 5",
      "1 3",
      "3 4",
      "3 1",
      "`Example Output 2`3",
      "5",
      "`Example Input 3`5",
      "1 85",
      "1 306",
      "1 345",
      "1 107",
      "1 193",
      "`Example Output 3`260",
      "459",
      "`Example Input 4`4",
      "1 1",
      "2 3",
      "3 2",
      "4 4",
      "`Example Output 4`3",
      "4",
      "`"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer NNN.\nNNN lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains two space-separated integers SiS_iSi​ and PiP_iPi​.",
    "outputFormat": "Print ⌊N2⌋\\left\\lfloor\\frac{N}{2}\\right\\rfloor⌊2N​⌋ lines. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines should contain a single integer ― the maximum beauty for at most iii pairs.",
